you observed, doubted,

578
00:25:36,218 --> 00:25:39,017
questioned, those kinds of emotions.

579
00:25:39,018 --> 00:25:41,217
This is training our

580
00:25:41,218 --> 00:25:42,818
observation skills.

581
00:25:47,738 --> 00:25:49,617
Okay, you remember,

582
00:25:49,618 --> 00:25:51,337
that moment just now?

583
00:25:51,338 --> 00:25:52,098
You had no idea,

584
00:25:52,099 --> 00:25:54,177
what my surprise would be.

585
00:25:54,178 --> 00:25:55,257
Then I did it again,

586
00:25:55,258 --> 00:25:56,018
and you didn't react.

587
00:25:56,019 --> 00:25:58,017
Completely different from last time.

588
00:25:58,018 --> 00:26:00,257
That's memory training for you.

589
00:26:00,258 --> 00:26:01,977
When I did that,

590
00:26:01,978 --> 00:26:03,697
what was going through your mind?

591
00:26:03,698 --> 00:26:05,657
It was sudden, unexpected.

592
00:26:05,658 --> 00:26:06,458
Got startled.

593
00:26:06,459 --> 00:26:08,337
This fresh memory

594
00:26:08,338 --> 00:26:09,697
has to live inside you.

595
00:26:09,698 --> 00:26:11,098
You have to be observant.

596
00:26:11,578 --> 00:26:14,297
Observation is a crucial quality,

597
00:26:14,298 --> 00:26:16,298
for a future professional actor.

598
00:26:18,098 --> 00:26:18,938
Next,

599
00:26:18,939 --> 00:26:20,697
we're moving on to

600
00:26:20,698 --> 00:26:22,937
our next segment.

601
00:26:22,938 --> 00:26:24,737
The next segment is

602
00:26:24,738 --> 00:26:26,698
an exam for you.

603
00:26:28,858 --> 00:26:31,177
With "Me" as the theme,

604
00:26:31,178 --> 00:26:33,137
structure a story.

605
00:26:33,138 --> 00:26:35,297
You have two hours to prepare.

606
00:26:35,298 --> 00:26:38,137
Independently create an original performance, no longer than four minutes.

607
00:26:38,138 --> 00:26:40,817
You may freely use props from the rehearsal hall.

608
00:26:40,818 --> 00:26:42,817
When time's up, return to the theater,

609
00:26:42,818 --> 00:26:43,818
for your performance.

610
00:26:43,938 --> 00:26:46,177
Sirs will score each performance,

611
00:26:46,178 --> 00:26:47,537
out of fifty points.

612
00:26:47,538 --> 00:26:49,737
The three students with the highest scores,

613
00:26:49,738 --> 00:26:51,377
will receive credit points as a reward.

614
00:26:51,378 --> 00:26:52,537
Credit points will affect

615
00:26:52,538 --> 00:26:55,218
your overall score in the Training Camp.

616
00:26:55,658 --> 00:26:57,297
Good luck to all of you!

617
00:26:57,298 --> 00:26:58,857
Thank you, Sir.

618
00:26:58,858 --> 00:26:59,858
See you in a bit!

619
00:27:01,978 --> 00:27:03,258
The topic is "Me".

620
00:27:05,818 --> 00:27:06,898
The pressure is on!

621
00:27:07,778 --> 00:27:09,457
I'm totally confused,

622
00:27:09,458 --> 00:27:10,258
and a bit panicked too.

623
00:27:10,258 --> 00:27:11,258
In such a short time,

624
00:27:11,259 --> 00:27:12,537
how am I supposed to portray it?

625
00:27:12,538 --> 00:27:14,178
How do I even approach this?

626
00:27:15,138 --> 00:27:17,337
Honestly, I was really stunned.

627
00:27:17,338 --> 00:27:19,817
It's like I didn't know what to do.

628
00:27:19,818 --> 00:27:23,057
Because having to perform as myself,

629
00:27:23,058 --> 00:27:25,217
I feel like I'm

630
00:27:25,218 --> 00:27:26,457
in some ways,

631
00:27:26,458 --> 00:27:27,818
the person who knows me the least.

632
00:27:28,578 --> 00:27:29,977
I've actually never acted before.

633
00:27:29,978 --> 00:27:30,898
I really can't

634
00:27:30,899 --> 00:27:32,538
think of what to do.
